From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Madar Operations <agostinialves@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Madar 2026-09-20 weekly addendum, counts refreshed 2026-09-27:
 issue 6 stated default C applied on its own date. The gate register has two
 homes and the workflow now says so - twelve build steps here, ten postbuild
 gates in package.json, 22 of 25 gating, and the three that do not with their
 reasons. Re-reconciled at the 09-27 review because the patch sat unapplied
 while four assertions landed and its own numbers went stale.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/.github/workflows/astro-pages.yml b/.github/workflows/astro-pages.yml
index 37b8383..bbe3f96 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/astro-pages.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/astro-pages.yml
@@ -136,6 +136,45 @@ jobs:
         # no stale dist to find — and the missing argument was the tell nobody
         # read. Ruling #51.
         run: python3 agents/tools/qa_jsonld.py web/dist
+      # ---- THE GATE REGISTER HAS TWO HOMES (issue #6, default C applied 2026-09-20) ----
+      #
+      # Reading this file top to bottom answers "what gates the deploy?" with TWELVE
+      # assertions. That is an incomplete answer and has been since 2026-09-14.
+      #
+      # The other TEN are gated from `postbuild` in web/package.json:
+      #   qa_css_tokens  qa_render  qa_arabic_shaping  qa_arabic_joining
+      #   qa_stable_order  qa_date_identity  qa_feed_enclosures  qa_chrome_links
+      #   qa_census  qa_packet_figures
+      #
+      # They are there rather than here because the autonomous identity that writes
+      # them is refused write access to .github/workflows/** - correctly; `workflows`
+      # is not a scope a workflow can grant itself. `npm run build` runs them, so they
+      # gate this job for real; they are simply declared somewhere else. Note that
+      # qa_packet_figures is handed the REPOSITORY ROOT, not dist - a distribution
+      # caption is never built - and sits in postbuild only because that is where a
+      # gate of this identity can be wired at all, not because it concerns the build.
+      #
+      # Issue #6 offered three options: a PAT with workflow scope (A), a human applying
+      # queued patches (B), or accepting package.json as a second equal home and saying
+      # so here (C). It carried a stated default - unanswered by the 2026-09-20 weekly
+      # review, apply C - and the date passed with no word. C is applied. The register
+      # is split, deliberately, and this comment is the thing that makes the split
+      # honest rather than hidden. (Issue #6 itself was CLOSED 2026-09-27 on its other
+      # limb: the run's pushes DO trigger the deploy, and always did - ruling #71. The
+      # two-homes fact this comment records is unaffected and still true.)
+      #
+      # TOTAL: 25 standing assertions, 22 of which gate the deploy.
+      # The three that do not: qa_live_drift and qa_sources_alive, named with their
+      # reasons in the paragraph below, and qa_feed_validators, whose reason cannot be
+      # written here because it belongs to the verify job - it lives in that tool's own
+      # header, and its one-line patch is queued beside this one.
+      #
+      # Counts re-reconciled 2026-09-27 against BOTH files. This comment was staged on
+      # 09-20 reading "seven / 21 / 19" and FOUR assertions landed while it sat in the
+      # queue unapplied - a staged patch is frozen prose about a moving count. If this
+      # ratio and the two files ever disagree, THE FILES ARE THE STATE and this comment
+      # is the stale one.
+      # -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
       # The last three hand-run assertions, wired 2026-09-13 (weekly review).
       # All three read only web/dist, all three have existed for weeks, all
       # three BIT HARD on first contact — qa_a11y_lang found 471 chrome strings
-- 
